---
_type: PltConcept
_label: 'Decidable proposition'
journey: fref("programming-language-theory/index.td")
status: 'reviewing'
tags:
  - 'logic'
---

A proposition $P$ for which an algorithm exists that, in finite time, either produces a proof of $P$ or a proof of $\neg P$ - i.e., you can compute which side of $P \vee \neg P$ holds.
